<title>UK: Barr &amp; Wallace Arnold H1 pretax profit up.</title>
<headline>Barr &amp; Wallace Arnold H1 pretax profit up.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		3.9		    vs 3.2</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.25		   vs 3.00</p>
<p> Pretax		     0.90		   vs 0.73</p>
<p> Turnover		   116.49		 vs 128.81</p>
<p> Operating profit	 1.63		   vs 1.18</p>
<p> Loss on disposal	 0.25		   vs nil</p>
<p> Interest payable	 0.48		   vs 0.45</p>
<p> Tax			  0.33		   vs 0.26</p>
<p> Net taxed		  0.58		   vs 0.47</p>
<p> Retained		   0.09		   vs 0.02</p>
<p> Pay date		   October 25</p>
<p>Div registration date  October 1  Ex-div date		September 23</p>
<p>NOTE - Motor retail and leisure group Barr &amp; Wallace Arnold Trust Plc said its increased dividend is a measure of its confidence in continuing improvement in financial performance.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
